1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,192
Is a word hard to understand, or does nobody actually know it?

2
00:00:05,392 --> 00:00:18,296
We often confuse things that are simply hidden or little-known with ideas that are incredibly complicated to understand. Today, let's learn how to choose the perfect everyday synonym to clear up this confusion.

3
00:00:18,496 --> 00:00:29,216
vague. Use when a statement or idea lacks clear details. For example: His explanation of the new rules was way too vague.

4
00:00:29,416 --> 00:00:33,992
Or: I only have a vague memory of what happened that night.

5
00:00:34,192 --> 00:00:45,800
complicated. Use when something is difficult to analyze or resolve. For example: The instructions for assembling this desk are incredibly complicated.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,392
Or: Solving this math equation is a very complicated process.

7
00:00:51,592 --> 00:01:01,832
unclear. Use when something is not easy to see or comprehend. For example: The road signs were unclear in the heavy rain.

8
00:01:02,032 --> 00:01:06,776
Or: It is still unclear who will win the election tomorrow.

9
00:01:06,976 --> 00:01:17,456
hidden. Use when something is kept out of sight or secret. For example: We discovered a hidden cabin deep inside the quiet forest.

10
00:01:17,656 --> 00:01:22,688
Or: The app has a hidden menu that most users never find.

11
00:01:22,888 --> 00:01:35,096
little-known. Use when describing a place, person, or fact unfamiliar to most. For example: He shared a little-known fact about the history of our town.

12
00:01:35,296 --> 00:01:40,472
Or: We decided to visit a little-known beach to avoid crowds.

13
00:01:40,672 --> 00:01:52,712
mysterious. Use when something is strange, exciting, and hard to explain. For example: A mysterious package arrived at my office door this morning.

14
00:01:52,912 --> 00:01:57,920
Or: The old house at the end of the street has a mysterious history.

15
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:12,104
Quick quiz! The speaker's directions to the conference hall were so blank that we got completely lost. A: vague … B: little-known … C: hidden

16
00:02:12,304 --> 00:02:20,480
The answer is vague. Vague fits perfectly because the directions lacked clear details, causing confusion.

17
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:25,280
Find hundreds more alternatives at another word for dot net.
